{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And He said: Who told you, etc.</b> Meaning: how did this moment differ from before it, when you stood before Me and did not feel your nakedness until now? On your own, this knowledge would not be newly acquired for you without someone telling you — hence His saying <b>Who told you</b>: through what means was this matter newly acquired in your knowledge? And according to what we explained, that his shame was from the sin, or from the diminishment of the spiritual apprehension of holiness and the covering of the cloud of glory, it would not be fitting to say 'Who told you'; rather, the Creator's intention was that He did not wish to disgrace him so utterly, and so He addressed him in this manner, 'Who told you,' as one asking a question. And there is substance to this question according to what we explained, that in the midst of this eating they realized that they were naked — for you must know that all the interpretations we offer according to the plain sense of the verses are all correct." "<b>From the tree, etc.</b> Here is an allusion that concerning the aspect of the tree HaShem also commanded him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:45.591721585Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}